Stage the frame journal's texture writes like its buffer writes (forge patch;
local Aurora-Viewer branch perf/metal-upload-writes, not upstream yet).

Queue::write_texture makes a staging buffer per call; on Metal each one is a
new allocation whose pages the CPU faults in as it fills them, which cost 4 to
9 ms of the render thread every few frames in a busy region (22 MB in a dozen
texture writes), up to 72 ms. The replay now copies the texture rows into the
journal's staging buffer at a copy's pitch and records a buffer-to-texture copy
in the journal's order. A frame over 32 MB stages what fits instead of sending
everything through the queue. AURORA_WRITE_STAGING=0 keeps upstream's path.

